WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
A medical diagnosis helps you decide what
to investigate.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.060
It does not tell you everything a person
can do.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.960
Chapter five connects medical and
psychiatric conditions with possible

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.920
communication and swallowing concerns.

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.480
Keep the word possible attached to those
associations.

6
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.680
A syndrome is a characteristic set of
symptoms.

7
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.580
The individual assessment establishes which
features are actually present

8
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.960
and how they affect function.

9
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.680
Start by following the relevant pathway.

10
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.200
Several conditions in the deck can affect
hearing, and hearing

11
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.980
difficulties can accompany speech and
language concerns.

12
00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.380
The slides place otitis media and
mastoiditis in that pathway.

13
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.980
Craniofacial conditions can direct
attention toward resonance, speech,

14
00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.200
feeding, and swallowing.

15
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.840
For example, the deck connects Pierre Robin
sequence with feeding

16
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.740
concerns, possible hearing related language
delays, and resonance issues

17
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.620
associated with cleft palate.

18
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.520
The condition guides the questions.

19
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.580
It does not replace hearing evidence or
direct examination.

20
00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.760
Neurological conditions can affect several
systems at once.

21
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:04.960
Stroke may involve language, speech motor
control, cognition, and swallowing.

22
00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.400
Parkinson's disease is associated in the
deck with dysarthria, swallowing

23
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.200
difficulty, and cognitive impairment.

24
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.180
Motor neuron disease can affect speech and
swallowing.

25
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.300
Developmental and learning conditions can
shift the focus toward language

26
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.320
learning, social communication, and
functional participation.

27
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.540
Similar concerns appear across different
diagnoses, so one symptom does

28
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.780
not identify its cause.

29
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.580
Turn each association into an assessment
question.

30
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.440
If hearing is a concern, what hearing
information is available?

31
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:38.180
If speech sounds different, is the issue
articulation, resonance, voice,

32
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.940
or a broader motor speech pattern?

33
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.720
If eating or drinking is difficult, what
swallowing assessment or

34
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.740
referral is indicated?

35
00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.220
Combine the history with relevant direct
evidence and information from

36
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:48.820
the team.

37
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.360
Use the condition directory to retrieve the
specific associations from

38
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.740
the slides, then return to the person in
front of

39
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:54.920
you.

40
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.520
The medical label points toward evidence
you need.

41
00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.400
It does not supply the answer in advance.
